       CoffeeLiqueur`Notebook`Cells`CellObj`$821]]}|>, 
 "Cells" -> {<|"Data" -> ".md\n# Recreation of World of Goo or Bridge \
Construction Game with WLJS\n\nHere we shall try to model a system of \
interconnected bonds using the Verlet method. Then, we'll add some visuals to \
make it feel like a game.\n\n<a href=\"#tldr-goo\">TLDR: actual \
game</a>\n\n<br/><br/>\n\n## Motion Equations\nThe system of connected points \
must obey Newton's laws and kinematic equations as well. To integrate them in \
real-time, Euler's method, RK (Runge-Kutta), or Verlet methods can be used. \
We will go for the Verlet method since it will be easier to apply constraints \
of the bonds in the future:\n\n$$\nx_{n+1} = 2 x_{n} - x_{n-1} + \
\\\\frac{f_{n}}{m} \\\\delta t^2\n$$", "Display" -> "codemirror", 
    "Hash" -> "47257693-cbf7-4c53-992a-8d2b9902e329", "Invisible" -> False, 
    "MetaOnly" -> False, "Props" -> <|"Hidden" -> True|>, 
    "PublicFields" -> {"Properties"}, "State" -> "Idle", "Type" -> "Input", 
    "UID" -> Null, "Notebook" -> "750b5a6f-68db-498f-89a6-d5e9974f261d"|>, 
   <|"Data" -> "# Recreation of World of Goo or Bridge Construction Game with \
WLJS\n\nHere we shall try to model a system of interconnected bonds using the \
Verlet method. Then, we'll add some visuals to make it feel like a \
game.\n\n<a href=\"#tldr-goo\">TLDR: actual game</a><br /><br />\n\n## Motion \
Equations\nThe system of connected points must obey Newton's laws and \
kinematic equations as well. To integrate them in real-time, Euler's method, \
RK (Runge-Kutta), or Verlet methods can be used. We will go for the Verlet \
method since it will be easier to apply constraints of the bonds in the \
future:\n\n$$\nx_{n+1} = 2 x_{n} - x_{n-1} + \\\\frac{f_{n}}{m} \\\\delta \
t^2\n$$", "Display" -> "markdown", "Hash" -> 
     "3dfdccef-1515-4d80-bf4e-121d47e8d962", "Invisible" -> False, 
    "MetaOnly" -> False, "Props" -> <||>, "PublicFields" -> {"Properties"}, 
    "State" -> "Idle", "Type" -> "Output", "UID" -> Null, 
    "Notebook" -> "750b5a6f-68db-498f-89a6-d5e9974f261d"|>, 
   <|"Data" -> ".md\nWe can try to apply it for the simples case, when \
$\\\\mathbf{f}_{n} = - m\\\\mathbf{x}/|\\\\mathbf{x}|^4$ is sort of a gravity \
force caused by a red star in the center", "Display" -> "codemirror", 
    "Hash" -> "e2d16b00-cb95-430e-b03f-64ddedd6ab71", "Invisible" -> False, 
    "MetaOnly" -> False, "Props" -> <|"Hidden" -> True|>, 
    "PublicFields" -> {"Properties"}, "State" -> "Idle", "Type" -> "Input", 
    "UID" -> Null, "Notebook" -> "750b5a6f-68db-498f-89a6-d5e9974f261d"|>, 
   <|"Data" -> "We can try to apply it for the simples case, when \
$\\\\mathbf{f}_{n} = - m\\\\mathbf{x}/|\\\\mathbf{x}|^4$ is sort of a gravity \
force caused by a red star in the center", "Display" -> "markdown", 
    "Hash" -> "5ae355ba-ed70-4086-88e1-a471a1b7e746", "Invisible" -> False, 
    "MetaOnly" -> False, "Props" -> <||>, "PublicFields" -> {"Properties"}, 
    "State" -> "Idle", "Type" -> "Output", "UID" -> Null, 
    "Notebook" -> "750b5a6f-68db-498f-89a6-d5e9974f261d"|>, 
   <|"Data" -> "estimateX[n_Integer, initialV_:0.01] := \
FixedPoint[Function[x,\n  {\n    2 x[[1]] - x[[2]] - 0.001 \
(*FB[*)((x[[1]])(*,*)/(*,*)((*SpB[*)Power[Norm[x[[1]]](*|*),(*|*)4](*]SpB*)))\
(*]FB*), \n    x[[1]], \n    x[[2]]\n  }\n], {\n  {-1.0, 2 initialV 0.01},\n  \
{-1.0, initialV 0.01},\n  {-1.0, 0}\n}, n];", "Display" -> "codemirror", 
